.TH "DRUNK" 7 "September 2025" "atomdns handlers" "atomdns authors"

.SH "DRUNK"
.SH "NAME"
.PP
\fIdrunk\fP \- test client behavior

.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fIdrunk\fP returns a static response to all queries, but the responses can be
delayed, dropped or truncated. The \fIdrunk\fP handler will respond to every A or
AAAA query. For any other type it will return a SERVFAIL response. The reply
for A will return 192.0.2.53 (RFC 5737
\[la]https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5737\[ra]),
for AAAA it returns 2001:DB8::53 (RFC 3849
\[la]https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3849\[ra]).

.SH "SYNTAX"
.PP
.RS

.nf
drunk {
    drop [/N]
    truncate [/M]
    delay [/L [DURATION]]
}

.fi
.RE

.IP \(bu 4
\fB\fCdrop\fR: drop every /\fBN\fP query, the default every second one (/2).
.IP \(bu 4
\fB\fCtruncate\fR: truncate every /\fBM\fP query, the default is /2.
.IP \(bu 4
\fB\fCdelay\fR: delay every /\fBL\fP query for \fBDURATION\fP, the default for is /22 and
the default for \fBDURATION\fP is 100ms.


.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
Drop every 1 in 3 queries to \fB\fCexample.org\fR:

.PP
.RS

.nf
example.org {
    drunk {
        drop /3
    }
}

.fi
.RE

.PP
Or even shorter if the defaults suit you. Note this only drops queries, it does not delay them.

.PP
.RS

.nf
example.org {
    drunk
}

.fi
.RE

.PP
Delay 1 in 3 queries for 50ms

.PP
.RS

.nf
example.org {
    drunk {
        delay /3 50ms
    }
}

.fi
.RE

.PP
Delay 1 in 3 and truncate 1 in 5.

.PP
.RS

.nf
example.org {
    drunk {
        delay /3 5ms
        truncate /5
    }
}

.fi
.RE
